-That is why a paprika extract should not be specified as though it were isolated capsanthin. The same specification describes a dark-red viscous liquid that is practically insoluble in water.[3] A supplier's “water-dispersible paprika” therefore needs its own composition and application description; the technical assessment explains that emulsifiers can be added to produce water-dispersible formulations.[2] Do not treat that description as proof of a transparent, molecularly dissolved colour.
